{"name":"Directoire Blue","hex":"#0061a8","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"directoire","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["Alternative form of Directoire."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/directoire"},{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"}],"entries":[{"title":"French Directory","blocks":[{"text":"The Directory was the system of government established by the French Constitution of \n1795. It takes its name from the committee of five men vested with executive power. The Directory governed the French First Republic from 26 October 1795 until 9 November 1799, when it was overthrown by Napoleon Bonaparte in the Coup of 18 Brumaire and replaced by the Consulate."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/c/c3/Flag_of_France.svg/330px-Flag_of_France.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/French_Directory"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Carte_de_France_divis%C3%A9e_suivant_les_quatre_d%C3%A9partements_de_Messieurs_les_secretaires_d%27Etat_-_par_Philippe_Buache_-_btv1b8593230j.jpg/500px-Carte_de_France_divis%C3%A9e_suivant_les_quatre_d%C3%A9partements_de_Messieurs_les_secretaires_d%27Etat_-_par_Philippe_Buache_-_btv1b8593230j.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Carte_de_France_divis%C3%A9e_suivant_les_quatre_d%C3%A9partements_de_Messieurs_les_secretaires_d%27Etat_-_par_Philippe_Buache_-_btv1b8593230j.jpg/1280px-Carte_de_France_divis%C3%A9e_suivant_les_quatre_d%C3%A9partements_de_Messieurs_les_secretaires_d%27Etat_-_par_Philippe_Buache_-_btv1b8593230j.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Carte_de_France_divis%C3%A9e_suivant_les_quatre_d%C3%A9partements_de_Messieurs_les_secretaires_d%27Etat_-_par_Philippe_Buache_-_btv1b8593230j.jpg/500px-Carte_de_France_divis%C3%A9e_suivant_les_quatre_d%C3%A9partements_de_Messieurs_les_secretaires_d%27Etat_-_par_Philippe_Buache_-_btv1b8593230j.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACarte_de_France_divis%C3%A9e_suivant_les_quatre_d%C3%A9partements_de_Messieurs_les_secretaires_d'Etat_-_par_Philippe_Buache_-_btv1b8593230j.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/Max_Adamo_Sturz_Robespierres.JPG/500px-Max_Adamo_Sturz_Robespierres.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1